{
  "id": "typescript-17-eslint-type-aware",
  "slug": "eslint-type-aware",
  "title": "ESLint type-aware rules and @typescript-eslint",
  "moduleId": "typescript-17-compiler-options-tooling",
  "order": 4,
  "hook": "**Type-aware ESLint** uses TS program for rules like **no-floating-promises** — needs parserOptions.project. Complements tsc, does not replace it.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "@typescript-eslint/parser + **recommendedTypeChecked** preset. **parserOptions.project** or **projectService** (TS 5.8+). Rules: no-floating-promises, no-misused-promises, no-unsafe-assignment. Separate fast vs typed lint in CI."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "typed lint",
              "longForm": "type-aware rules",
              "plainDefinition": "Rules using type checker.",
              "example": "no-floating-promises"
            },
            {
              "term": "parserOptions.project",
              "longForm": "tsconfig for eslint",
              "plainDefinition": "Program for rules.",
              "example": "tsconfig.eslint.json"
            },
            {
              "term": "recommended-type-checked",
              "longForm": "preset",
              "plainDefinition": "Curated typed rules.",
              "example": "typescript-eslint preset"
            },
            {
              "term": "projectService",
              "longForm": "TS 5.8",
              "plainDefinition": "Faster project service API.",
              "example": "projectService true"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "tsc misses unawaited promises. Misconfigured project globs false negatives. Senior CI splits lint stages."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: eslint replaces tsc",
          "body": "Run tsc --noEmit AND typed eslint — different jobs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "install typescript-eslint",
              "body": "See code walkthrough and official documentation for this step."
            },
            {
              "title": "tsconfig.eslint.json",
              "body": "include tests"
            },
            {
              "title": "recommendedTypeChecked",
              "body": "See code walkthrough and official documentation for this step."
            },
            {
              "title": "parallel CI jobs",
              "body": "fast+typed"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "typed eslint",
            "source": "flowchart LR\n  SRC --> ESL\n  TSC[TS Program] --> ESL\n  ESL --> RULES"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "javascript",
            "label": "flat config typed",
            "code": "import tseslint from \"typescript-eslint\";\nexport default tseslint.config(\n  ...tseslint.configs.recommendedTypeChecked,\n  { languageOptions: { parserOptions: { projectService: true, tsconfigRootDir: import.meta.dirname } } },\n);",
            "explanation": "Type-checked preset."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "floating promise",
            "code": "async function save() { return fetch(\"/api\"); }\nfunction click() { save(); } // eslint error\nasync function fixed() { await save(); }",
            "explanation": "tsc allows — eslint catches."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "misused promises",
            "code": "async function ok() { return true; }\nif (ok()) {} // eslint: Promise always truthy\nif (await ok()) {}",
            "explanation": "async in if without await."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "json",
            "label": "tsconfig.eslint.json",
            "code": "{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n  \"include\": [\"src\", \"tests\", \"*.config.ts\"]\n}",
            "explanation": "All linted files in program."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
